  "notes": "West leads the ♥8 against 4♠. East wins and continues the suit, South ruffing. To make the contract spades must be 3-2. South must hold his club losers to 1.\n\nTrying to ruff a club in dummy will be fatal if East has 3 spades. If South plays clubs before drawing 2 rounds of trump, East will win and promote a second trump trick with a heart return. If South draws 2 rounds of trump before playing clubs as before, East will win the ♣A and draw dummy's last trump.\n\nIn order to guard against the above layout, South must lead a low club from the dummy after drawing 2 rounds of trump. East must duck and South wins the ♣K. South will no longer be able to ruff a club in dummy, but he can now succeed via a dummy reversal.\n\nSouth crosses to dummy in diamonds and ruffs a heart. South next crosses again in diamonds. East must pitch or South will be able to ruff his club loser in dummy. Dummy's last heart is played and ruffed by South.\n\nSouth continues diamonds allowing East to ruff whenever he chooses. South will lose a trump trick and the ♣A at the end. If West started with the third spade, he cannot gain by overruffing when South is ruffing North's hearts. South will still be able to score the remaining trumps separately and lose just 3 tricks.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥8 against 4♠. East wins and continues the suit, South ruffing. To make the contract spades must be 3-2. South must hold his club losers to 1.",
    "Trying to ruff a club in dummy will be fatal if East has 3 spades. If South plays clubs before drawing 2 rounds of trump, East will win and promote a second trump trick with a heart return. If South draws 2 rounds of trump before playing clubs as before, East will win the ♣A and draw dummy's last trump.",
    "In order to guard against the above layout, South must lead a low club from the dummy after drawing 2 rounds of trump. East must duck and South wins the ♣K. South will no longer be able to ruff a club in dummy, but he can now succeed via a dummy reversal.",
    "South crosses to dummy in diamonds and ruffs a heart. South next crosses again in diamonds. East must pitch or South will be able to ruff his club loser in dummy. Dummy's last heart is played and ruffed by South.",
    "South continues diamonds allowing East to ruff whenever he chooses. South will lose a trump trick and the ♣A at the end. If West started with the third spade, he cannot gain by overruffing when South is ruffing North's hearts. South will still be able to score the remaining trumps separately and lose just 3 tricks."
  ],
